       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg daily is three times the maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **50 mg once daily** is the usual starting dose for depression, anxiety, and similar indications. Some indications start lower, at 25 mg.\n- **100\u2013200 mg once daily** is the range for patients who need titration after a trial at a lower dose.\n- **60 mg**, if this was a typo for 50 or 100 mg.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and indication with your supervising resident or attending. Once you have the corrected dose, I'll enter it right away. If a dose above 200 mg is truly intended, which would be highly unusual, the attending should place or co-sign it with documented justification."
