       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 600 mg daily. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. The dose is three times the 200 mg/day maximum, and I have no indication or rationale that would justify it. A medical student also shouldn't be the one to place an order this far outside the labeled range.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Escalate to your attending or resident.** If they want a dose above 200 mg, they can enter it themselves with documented justification. Pharmacy will probably want to review it too.\n- **Ask pharmacy** for a dosing consult if there's a specific clinical reason, such as a prior partial response or a drug interaction affecting levels.\n- **Let me enter a standard dose now.** For example, 50 mg once daily, or 100\u2013200 mg once daily if the patient is already titrated. Tell me the dose and indication and I'll place it.\n\nIf I've misunderstood the situation, for example if the order was meant for a different drug or unit, tell me and I'll re-check."
